    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey im getting this SettingWithCopyWarning in my notebook and it's driving me crazy. i'm trying to filter a df and then add a column to the slice but it keeps throwing this warning. here is the code:\n\ndf_subset = df[df['category'] == 'electronics']\ndf_subset['price_plus_tax'] = df_subset['price'] * 1.1\n\nwhy does pandas keep complaining and how do i fix it properly?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This warning occurs because Pandas suspects you are modifying a view of the original DataFrame (`df`) rather than an independent copy, which can lead to unpredictable behavior. The proper way to fix this is by explicitly creating a copy of the filtered DataFrame using `.copy()` right after filtering. Change `df_subset = df[df['category'] == 'electronics']` to `df_subset = df[df['category'] == 'electronics'].copy()`, and the warning should disappear.",
      "source": "target",
